# The built binary. Anchored with a leading slash, or the bare name also
# matches the cmd DIRECTORY and quietly excludes the whole command from the
# repository.
# Built binaries. Anchored with a leading slash so the name cannot also match a
# directory. Both names are listed: the old one stays here so that a stale
# ff.exe left over from before the rename can never be committed by accident —
# which is exactly what happened the moment this line was changed.
/fastfind
/fastfind.exe
/ff
/ff.exe
/dist/

# Go
*.test
*.out
